{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people","id":1140049,"title":"[Lunars] How do shamans, tricksters, and warriors heal people?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-13T17:59:39-07:00","id":1140049,"title":"[Lunars] How do shamans, tricksters, and warriors heal people?","content":"Here are some ideas. Please tell me what you think, and share your own!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Feed a Fever, Starve a Cold / Good For What Ails You</b><br /> <br /> After properly diagnosing someone's sickness, roll (Intelligence + Medicine) to intuitively understand which of the many things you've eaten in your life would prove most nutritional or medicinal for your patient; add (Essence) automatic successes if you have suffered that specific disease before. With one success, the ingredients are extremely time-consuming and dangerous to hunt, requiring at least a week's time. With two or three successes, the ingredients require only a few days at most. With five or more successes, the ingredients are things that you can gather within the hour.<br /> <br /> After gathering the ingredients, begin a minor Intelligence-based Crafting project to produce the meal or medicine. Supernatural diseases demand a major project. After eating the meal, the patient adds the Crafting threshold successes to their next Resistance roll against the disease's morbidity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>You Are What You Eat</b><br /> <br /> Kill and butcher the strongest animals you can find. Make the heartiest meals. Feed your patient well, so that they may recover faster from injury. Aggravated injuries require a major cooking Crafting project, and are converted into lethal wounds before any lethal wounds are healed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lick Wounds</b><br /> <br /> Supplement the (Intelligence + Medicine) action to staunch someone's bleeding (lethal) wounds, without needing bandages, tools, or medicine. With any success, the wounds are at least sterilized. Threshold successes will convert those lethal wounds into bashing if the patient spent the remainder of the day resting in bed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mother's Touch</b><br /> <br /> Even without diagnosing the patient's wound or illness, spend at least two hours a day making them as comfortable as possible, keeping them company, raising their spirits, and distracting them from their pain. For as long as you maintain the commitment of motes and time, reduce their wound penalties and add +2 to their Resistance checks against disease. Each day, you may re-roll a failed or botched diagnosis roll as continued observation and conversation reveals new details.<br /> <br /> This Charm can also be used to treat Derangements directly, even while taking care of a physical ailment. Derangements require a (Perception or Intelligence + Socialize) to diagnose and an extended (Charisma + Presence or Socialize) roll to treat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Placebo Effect</b><br /> <br /> You can convince someone that they've been poisoned, causing them pain with harmless water, or greater pain with actual poison. By the same token, you can reduce someone's pain by making them think you've handled them actually efficacious medicine, or relieve even more pain than the medicine would actually handle on its own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Veil of Sleep</b><br /> <br /> Hypnotize the willing, putting them in a relaxed, suggestive state which allows you to command them to sleep. Thus can you help them escape their pain and rest. Or you can use their suggestive state to deal with their Derangements.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you can hypnotize an enemy, you can use that vulnerability to harm them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Suck Out Poison</b><br /> <br /> The Lunar requires a proper medical diagnosis to known where to bite. Each success on a (??? + Medicine) roll helps take away a dose of the diagnosed poison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Do That Voodoo You Do So Well</b><br /> <br /> Take someone's Heart's Blood without killing them. Wear their face when they're sick or injured. Fool Heaven so that it cannot distinguish their Fate from yours.<br /> <br /> As long as you remain close to your patient, the two of you share Health Levels. You both divide wound penalties and doses of poison between you. You both become infected with any diseases the other had, but you both Resist them together. If they are too weak to eat, you can eat their share for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demons Is Cheating</b><br /> <br /> Summon Stomach Bottle-Beetle. Optionally, eat it so that you can become it without needing to bothering with a summoning or a number of other Lunar Charms ever again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T20:35:54-07:00","id":1140074,"title":"","content":"I like all these options.<br /> The real-world shamanic tradition would be to call out the evil spirit that's causing the illness or find whatever sorcerer has stolen their soul and do spiritual battle. That seems more like a Sidereal Charm, though, and I think Terminate Illness references it in the fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T21:25:19-07:00","id":1140079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140074#post1140074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real-world shamanic tradition would be to call out the evil spirit that's causing the illness or find whatever sorcerer has stolen their soul and do spiritual battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured. But that doesn't work when most of the time, disease has nothing to do with spirits at all.<br /> <br /> There's the alternative of stuffing spirits INTO sick people to heal them, but even if you start out with enough spirits in the area to make that work, they'll probably start making themselves scarce when you're around.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I really liked the idea of finding more ways to work &quot;hunting&quot; into Lunar stories. How much time do you spend killing beasts to roast their meat in games like <i>Monster Hunter</i> and <i>Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T23:17:54-07:00","id":1140096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140079#post1140079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I figured. But that doesn't work when most of the time, disease has nothing to do with spirits at all.<br /> <br /> There's the alternative of stuffing spirits INTO sick people to heal them, but even if you start out with enough spirits in the area to make that work, they'll probably start making themselves scarce when you're around.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I really liked the idea of finding more ways to work &quot;hunting&quot; into Lunar stories. How much time do you spend killing beasts to roast their meat in games like <i>Monster Hunter</i> and <i>Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>There ARE supposed to be disease spirits. So natural summoning of the god/spirit and battling to weaken the disease can work. I had something in my attempts at making Solar's doctors as to &quot;no you can't have a cleric, this isn't D&amp;D do this slow and ardous and all healing is down by super duper magic. Sheesh. Yeah dragonblooded regenerate in a bath why you ask?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm okay with that idea. Obviously the problem is that opens to &quot;GM can set things however they damn please&quot; and like most serious medicine plots make it need mountain lottuses or something.<br /> <br /> Then again chase, negotiate, fight, or invite the disease seem safe enough. From feeding it some of you to strengthen to inviting the disease in.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;why take it if the Exalted can fight it off&quot; Gods are genuinely weird in their thinking. Getting beaten by an Exalted and getting to feed off of SOME of their essence for the struggle is decent enough for some. For them its a more of a boxing match than life or death struggle, perhaps.<br /> <br /> Overall all these seem okay except the face stealing part of the &quot;share &quot; charm. Sucking out poison I feel should be easy. As is developing antivenom/resistance once sufferred or exposed. This does run the issue of making it so you pay for a charm just to have to work hard to fulfill out its use.<br /> does that work for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T02:11:35-07:00","id":1140116,"title":"","content":"By default killing a disease god does nothing to the disease, the river god is not the river etc. I suppose there could be a power that would make it so killing a cholera god does cure cholera, or perhaps evokes the disease from a person into some kind of elemental that you could then kill. <br /> You can, at the moment, find a disease god and intimidate it into weakening the disease in a sufferer. Well, when all you have is a Deadly Beastman Transformation...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T02:36:46-07:00","id":1140121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140074#post1140074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real-world shamanic tradition would be to call out the evil spirit that's causing the illness or find whatever sorcerer has stolen their soul and do spiritual battle. That seems more like a Sidereal Charm, though, and I think Terminate Illness references it in the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that kind of thing would inform the imagery of a Charm, without it being a matter of literally doing battle with something that doesn't really exist in this cosmology.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T05:45:47-07:00","id":1140139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140116#post1140116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default killing a disease god does nothing to the disease, the river god is not the river etc. I suppose there could be a power that would make it so killing a cholera god does cure cholera, or perhaps evokes the disease from a person into some kind of elemental that you could then kill. <br /> You can, at the moment, find a disease god and intimidate it into weakening the disease in a sufferer. Well, when all you have is a Deadly Beastman Transformation...</div> </div> </div> </div>What he said.<br /> <br /> There isn't a disease god for every infection in the world. One disease god in an area simply reports to YuShan about all infections in its sphere of responsibility. Diseases start and spread regardless of the God. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140121#post1140121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think that kind of thing would inform the imagery of a Charm, without it being a matter of literally doing battle with something that doesn't really exist in this cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is possible, but what DOES that look like, and what would it actually be doing for the Lunar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T06:48:32-07:00","id":1140151,"title":"","content":"I think a better approach would be to challenge/battle the god of a given disease where if the Lunar wins, they remove the disease from the person. Killing the god wouldn't cure the victim, but the god likely has the power to abate it.<br /> <br /> That said, I like the ideas you put in here Sunder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T08:14:52-07:00","id":1140170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140139#post1140139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is possible, but what DOES that look like</div> </div> </div> </div>Some kind of chanting and gesturing, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what would it actually be doing for the Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMechanically? If it's disease, I'd say something that is a bit hefty in mote cost, but cures immediately might be fitting.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm thinking about descriptions given of how different Exalted dealt with the Great Contagion, in addition to looking at the Solar Medicine Charms. On the one hand, in Solar Medicine, I see some effects that not only heal, but empower being a physician in a manner that can help chain together a sequence of treatments. With ideas of Lunars struggling against the Contagion because that kind of healing is not really in their wheelhouse, I feel as though their approaches should be direct and powerful, but limited in scope, not have a large place in their powers and lack internal supports to expand their range.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T08:49:23-07:00","id":1140181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140151#post1140151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a better approach would be to challenge/battle the god of a given disease where if the Lunar wins, they remove the disease from the person. Killing the god wouldn't cure the victim, but the god likely has the power to abate it.<br /> <br /> That said, I like the ideas you put in here Sunder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like my ideas, because *any* Exalt could hunt down and coerce a disease spirit like that. Doing things like that was a big part of why the Sidereals developed the Immaculate Dragon Styles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140170#post1140170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some kind of chanting and gesturing, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Performance action. A performance might be part of tricking someone with the Placebo Effect, or entertaining and distracting someone with Mother's Touch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bMechanically? If it's disease, I'd say something that is a bit hefty in mote cost, but cures immediately might be fitting.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm thinking about descriptions given of how different Exalted dealt with the Great Contagion, in addition to looking at the Solar Medicine Charms. On the one hand, in Solar Medicine, I see some effects that not only heal, but empower being a physician in a manner that can help chain together a sequence of treatments. With ideas of Lunars struggling against the Contagion because that kind of healing is not really in their wheelhouse, I feel as though their approaches should be direct and powerful, but limited in scope, not have a large place in their powers and lack internal supports to expand their range. </div> </div> </div>Big heals with poor endurance and scalability? Maybe.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want Lunar Charms to combine with each other for greater effects like Solar Charms do... just not necessarily toward the same ends.<br /> <br /> That's something I was trying to get at by tying Lunar healing with Lunar crafting and also Lunar hunting. If Solar Medicine rewards Solar Medicine, I'd like to see Lunar activities in one field reward Lunar activities in other fields.<br /> <br /> The Solar Specialist (reinforced by their new Supernal mechanic) versus the Lunar Generalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T08:51:59-07:00","id":1140184,"title":"","content":"what if you made the diesease into an entity to battle or hunt? Not a diesease god, but a spirit that was the particular case of the disesease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:08:23-07:00","id":1140195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140184#post1140184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what if you made the diesease into an entity to battle or hunt? Not a diesease god, but a spirit that was the particular case of the disesease.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be concerned wih what other things Lunars could transform into creatures which are capable of putting up meaningful fights against Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:26:43-07:00","id":1140204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140184#post1140184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what if you made the diesease into an entity to battle or hunt? Not a diesease god, but a spirit that was the particular case of the disesease.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just about to propose the same thing. Wouldn't even have to be a disease. Any injury, pull out and form a living representation of this malady, and destroy it to abate the effects of it, or feed it to make them worse...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140195#post1140195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be concerned wih what other things Lunars could transform into creatures which are capable of putting up meaningful fights against Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they aren't inherently fully autonomous and real to begin with. You pull out a little creature representing some poor schlub's syphilis, but that creature is limited in what it can interact with, and where it can even go to start.<br /> <br /> Upgrade charms could allow you to allow these manifestations to have lasting effects on the surrounding environs, or even transfer them into another host.<br /> <br /> Just got the cool idea of an intentionally diseased lunar that pulls out their malady monsters to do battle for them. Pertussis I choose you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:30:30-07:00","id":1140206,"title":"","content":"I remember Netsilik (I think, maybe it was a different Inuit tribe) shamans pulled out bloody worms that were the cause of the illness, Kung shamans removed arrows from the sick's bodies, and so on. So maybe objects, if not full on creatures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:39:26-07:00","id":1140212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140206#post1140206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Netsilik (I think, maybe it was a different Inuit tribe) shamans pulled out bloody worms that were the cause of the illness, Kung shamans removed arrows from the sick's bodies, and so on. So maybe objects, if not full on creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like running an egg all over someones body to pull the sickness out and then crushing it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T10:42:58-07:00","id":1140234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people#post1140049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are some ideas. Please tell me what you think, and share your own!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Feed a Fever, Starve a Cold / Good For What Ails You</b><br /> <br /> After properly diagnosing someone's sickness, roll (Intelligence + Medicine) to intuitively understand which of the many things you've eaten in your life would prove most nutritional or medicinal for your patient; add (Essence) automatic successes if you have suffered that specific disease before. With one success, the ingredients are extremely time-consuming and dangerous to hunt, requiring at least a week's time. With two or three successes, the ingredients require only a few days at most. With five or more successes, the ingredients are things that you can gather within the hour.<br /> <br /> After gathering the ingredients, begin a minor Intelligence-based Crafting project to produce the meal or medicine. Supernatural diseases demand a major project. After eating the meal, the patient adds the Crafting threshold successes to their next Resistance roll against the disease's morbidity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>You Are What You Eat</b><br /> <br /> Kill and butcher the strongest animals you can find. Make the heartiest meals. Feed your patient well, so that they may recover faster from injury. Aggravated injuries require a major cooking Crafting project, and are converted into lethal wounds before any lethal wounds are healed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lick Wounds</b><br /> <br /> Supplement the (Intelligence + Medicine) action to staunch someone's bleeding (lethal) wounds, without needing bandages, tools, or medicine. With any success, the wounds are at least sterilized. Threshold successes will convert those lethal wounds into bashing if the patient spent the remainder of the day resting in bed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mother's Touch</b><br /> <br /> Even without diagnosing the patient's wound or illness, spend at least two hours a day making them as comfortable as possible, keeping them company, raising their spirits, and distracting them from their pain. For as long as you maintain the commitment of motes and time, reduce their wound penalties and add +2 to their Resistance checks against disease. Each day, you may re-roll a failed or botched diagnosis roll as continued observation and conversation reveals new details.<br /> <br /> This Charm can also be used to treat Derangements directly, even while taking care of a physical ailment. Derangements require a (Perception or Intelligence + Socialize) to diagnose and an extended (Charisma + Presence or Socialize) roll to treat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Placebo Effect</b><br /> <br /> You can convince someone that they've been poisoned, causing them pain with harmless water, or greater pain with actual poison. By the same token, you can reduce someone's pain by making them think you've handled them actually efficacious medicine, or relieve even more pain than the medicine would actually handle on its own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Veil of Sleep</b><br /> <br /> Hypnotize the willing, putting them in a relaxed, suggestive state which allows you to command them to sleep. Thus can you help them escape their pain and rest. Or you can use their suggestive state to deal with their Derangements.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you can hypnotize an enemy, you can use that vulnerability to harm them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Suck Out Poison</b><br /> <br /> The Lunar requires a proper medical diagnosis to known where to bite. Each success on a (??? + Medicine) roll helps take away a dose of the diagnosed poison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Do That Voodoo You Do So Well</b><br /> <br /> Take someone's Heart's Blood without killing them. Wear their face when they're sick or injured. Fool Heaven so that it cannot distinguish their Fate from yours.<br /> <br /> As long as you remain close to your patient, the two of you share Health Levels. You both divide wound penalties and doses of poison between you. You both become infected with any diseases the other had, but you both Resist them together. If they are too weak to eat, you can eat their share for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demons Is Cheating</b><br /> <br /> Summon Stomach Bottle-Beetle. Optionally, eat it so that you can become it without needing to bothering with a summoning or a number of other Lunar Charms ever again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like all of these thematically. <br /> <br /> In the absence of playtestting I won't comment mechanically..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:09:39-07:00","id":1140389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140204#post1140204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just about to propose the same thing. Wouldn't even have to be a disease. Any injury, pull out and form a living representation of this malady, and destroy it to abate the effects of it, or feed it to make them worse...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the Sidereal Exalted are the ones who work with intangible qualities as if they were tangible things. Name-Stealing Practice?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe they aren't inherently fully autonomous and real to begin with. You pull out a little creature representing some poor schlub's syphilis, but that creature is limited in what it can interact with, and where it can even go to start. </div> </div> </div>Then how are they a threat worth the effort of a fight scene?<br /> <br /> If they don't demand a fight scene to kill, then making the disease monster is pure fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:56:38-07:00","id":1140402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140389#post1140389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the Sidereal Exalted are the ones who work with intangible qualities as if they were tangible things. Name-Stealing Practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because one splat can do a given action doesn't mean all splats are proscribed from capability in that action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T08:34:54-07:00","id":1140523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140389#post1140389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the Sidereal Exalted are the ones who work with intangible qualities as if they were tangible things. Name-Stealing Practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it is the difference between associated Auspices of Fate, and mystic associations. More folklore, less riddle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140389#post1140389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then how are they a threat worth the effort of a fight scene?<br /> <br /> If they don't demand a fight scene to kill, then making the disease monster is pure fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't say you had to have a knock down drag out brawl with someone's head cold, just confront them. A battle of wits and or wills.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to go the physical route, which is a-okay in my book, it could only be tangible to the victim and the Lunar. Minor sickness and injuries would barely necessitate a roll, but wanting to weaken or destroy the final stage leprosy of the benevolent philosopher-king, that could be a real challenge.<br /> <br /> I thought your initial comment about this challenging an Exalt was crying foul on a Lunar creating viable disease minions to attack their Exalted foes, not trying to make an interesting scene for the Lunar healer themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T08:48:02-07:00","id":1140527,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda drawn to the idea of the lunar forcing a physical manifestation of a disease/injury and confronting it. I am also drawn to the idea that sometimes really young lunars (or lunars who roll just super shitty) fuck this up and the disease/injury wins and then gets let loose from the body to rampage through the countryside. <br /> <br /> This could also happen if the lunar tries to treat something they think is innocuous like a cold or something and it actually turns out it's the black death or the contagion returned or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:39:53-07:00","id":1140549,"title":"","content":"So, could Lunars thus produce artifacts by dreaming of the finished product and then go hunting it through a fantasy world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T11:43:46-07:00","id":1140577,"title":"","content":"That seems like a few leaps too many IMO, but you do you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:08:30-07:00","id":1140634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140577#post1140577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a few leaps too many IMO, but you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just trying to understand the limits other people see on the Lunar Exalted ability to create tangible things from intangible conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:25:02-07:00","id":1140642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140634#post1140634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just trying to understand the limits other people see on the Lunar Exalted ability to create tangible things from intangible conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Understandable.<br /> <br /> First leap, for me, is going from an illness, which is a tangible thing, to something imagined.<br /> <br /> Second, instead of creating something that represents a tangible, or now imagined, thing, we are creating that object.<br /> <br /> Third, not only are we creating an object, we are creating an artifact, presumably with some magical materials also being created wholesale.<br /> <br /> At this point it's just WST with less steps and drawbacks.<br /> <br /> Bringing it back to &quot;limits [sic] other people see on the Lunar Exalted&quot;, I was directly drawing from shamanistic practices of confronting malign affects on the body through mysticism. I don't see dreaming up a cool sword and then waking up with a cool sword as a shamanistic practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:30:59-07:00","id":1140645,"title":"","content":"Okay, so start with the components to make a mundane sword, which are tangible things.<br /> <br /> Second, create a creature which represents the finished sword or its current raw ingredients.<br /> <br /> Now hunt down the single or multiple beasts, as you would a disease-beast.<br /> <br /> You kill the representative beast to achieve the desired change upon the world. An illness is destroyed, a sword is made.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, if you want to stick to destroying conditions relating to persons, would you accept that whole process as a way to make someone stop loving someone you hate or hating someone you love, by killing a representation of that Intimacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T15:11:11-07:00","id":1140656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140645#post1140645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, if you want to stick to destroying conditions relating to persons, would you accept that whole process as a way to make someone stop loving someone you hate or hating someone you love, by killing a representation of that Intimacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the brainpower to devote to whether or not this is in house for Lunars right now, but it's <i>awesome</i> and <i>someone</i> has to be able to do it.<br /> EDIT: To actually contribute something to the discussion wrt Sidereals and Lunars: Sidereals can do stuff like steal your name because they're all about abstract and metaphysical things. If Lunars do such things, it's instead because they're all about getting physical with things, even things that shouldn't be physical with. I don't know if that's a helpful distinction in the end, but it's how I understand it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":1797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","user":"Ellis","date":". 09-15-2017, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T16:15:13-07:00","id":1140670,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... not really &quot;healing&quot; as such, but would bestowing herd/tribal immunity be in the Lunar charm wheelhouse? As in, people who do certain thing (eg initiation ritual), or have a certain item (eg tribal totem) or share a certain Intimacy (loyalty to the tribe or ideal) gain immunity from certain conditions for as long as the Lunar commits Essence to the charm. Would that work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T16:41:43-07:00","id":1140671,"title":"","content":"What if the Lunar sat next to the patient and entered a meditative trance where her spirit enters the Essence of the patient?<br /> <br /> She perceives his injuried body as a damaged web, and uses her Int+Med to intuitively understand how to mend the weave.<br /> <br /> She sees a disease as a monster, and if she diagnosed it first then she is prepared to fight it and scores an ambush attack with Int+Med before the battle begins in earnest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T10:00:35-07:00","id":1140849,"title":"","content":"The same principle could be applied to repairing Artifacts. The Lunar meditates, sends his spirit inside the Essence of the artifact, and attempts to affect repairs upon the metaphorical landscape around him through his understanding of Craft (and Lore and Occult).<br /> <br /> The same Charm might be used to fundamentally alter a moonsilver Artifact's nature, allowing you to scrap a powerbow to build a new daiklaive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T10:15:41-07:00","id":1140855,"title":"","content":"If a Solar can have a Mind Palace library, a Lunar oughta be able to sneak into it to assassinate the manifestation of the Solar's depression, after which the Solar will begin slowly recovering from their malaise. And if they can do it to a Solar, they oughta be able to do it to mortals easy.<br /> <br /> I would say Lunars are more likely to treat diseases via shamanic practices than Medicine directly: summon forth and defeat or bargain with or trick your friendly neighborhood Influenza Deity, rather than grind herbs or put pins in sacred meridians on the human body to promote healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T21:35:42-07:00","id":1140976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1140402#post1140402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because one splat can do a given action doesn't mean all splats are proscribed from capability in that action.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be transparent, I don't mean to ignore this point.<br /> <br /> I simply don't have a counter-argument that seems well-reasoned enough to be worth sharing.<br /> <br /> If I ever do, I'll post it.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination?p=1140982#post1140982\">Oh wait, I remembered something.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 09-17-2017, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T06:20:45-07:00","id":1141721,"title":"","content":"Oh, goodness. I looked at my last ideas and remembered something. <br /> <br /> Who here has ever played Disgaea?<br /> <br /> It's a turn-based strategy RPG with absolutely ludicrous level caps and grinding systems.<br /> <br /> You can actually enter &quot;dungeons&quot; within your own items, and improve the quality of the items by defeating all of the enemies of every floor in the item until the item acknowledges you as its master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:16:00-07:00","id":1141755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people?p=1141721#post1141721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, goodness. I looked at my last ideas and remembered something.<br /> <br /> Who here has ever played Disgaea?<br /> <br /> It's a turn-based strategy RPG with absolutely ludicrous level caps and grinding systems.<br /> <br /> You can actually enter &quot;dungeons&quot; within your own items, and improve the quality of the items by defeating all of the enemies of every floor in the item until the item acknowledges you as its master.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the shamanistic themes we're discussing, I could totally see this as a way for a lunar to gain evocations from an artifact. Or perhaps even part of the lunar craft process. Sounds a lot cooler than banging a hammer on an anvil for a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T09:18:31-07:00","id":1143812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1140049-lunars-how-do-shamans-tricksters-and-warriors-heal-people#post1140049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Do That Voodoo You Do So Well</b><br /> <br /> Take someone's Heart's Blood without killing them. Wear their face when they're sick or injured. Fool Heaven so that it cannot distinguish their Fate from yours.<br /> <br /> As long as you remain close to your patient, the two of you share Health Levels. You both divide wound penalties and doses of poison between you. You both become infected with any diseases the other had, but you both Resist them together. If they are too weak to eat, you can eat their share for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's return to this idea.<br /> <br /> When the Lunar takes someone's Heart's Blood, he takes their Essence or spirit into his own. He makes them a part of his own power, his own body.<br /> <br /> I wrote a post about how, similar to how Liminal Charms represent techniques for elementally controlling the physical, visceral substances of corpses and their own bodies, Lunar Charms represent techniques for harnessing the power, rage, and insight of their bestial Totemic Spirits, as well as the other spirits they have taken into themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1143102-external-vs-internal-the-focus-of-an-exaltation-s-essence?p=1143360#post1143360\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1143102-external-vs-internal-the-focus-of-an-exaltation-s-essence?p=1143360#post1143360\"> Why each Exalted Host can do things like no one else can - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1143102-external-vs-internal-the-focus-of-an-exaltation-s-essence?p=1143360#post1143360\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1143102-external-vs-internal-the-focus-of-an-exaltation-s-essence?p=1143360#post1143360 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \u200bOr: &amp;quot;What your Excellency says about you!&amp;quot; The following are my own opinions based on my understanding and interpretations of the canon material. I'd </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is the heart of Lunar Shamanism. Not simply the power to deal with gods and elementals and ghosts, but to deal with the spirits of living creatures. Their own inner beasts, and the spirits of the prey they have conquered, or the wards who have given themselves over to Lunar dominion and mercy.<br /> <br /> So, what if Heart's Blood empowered - or even allowed in the first place - the meditative spirit-questing healing ritual?<br /> <br /> What if any similar ritual regarding the creation or repair of Artifacts depended on the Lunar owning the Heart's Blood of the creature that he killed for the necessary exotic components?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}